From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: castledking <thecastledking@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 04:02:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Optimise brain ticking

Brain#tick walked a TreeMap of HashMaps of LinkedHashSets to start
behaviours, then walked it again to find the running ones, for every mob
with a brain on every tick. With a thousand villagers that walk was about
a quarter of the tick. Keep the same behaviours in arrays built from those
maps, in exactly the order the walk visits them, and rebuild the arrays
whenever the maps change.

The active activities are still checked group by group while behaviours
are started, so a behaviour that switches the brain to another activity
part way through, like a villager starting to panic, is honoured exactly
as before. Lithium's and Leaf's versions of this cache the active
behaviours for the whole pass, which does not keep that.

Sensors and memory slots are also ticked from arrays, memories are kept in
an identity map, and GateBehavior walks its children by index.

